# ===================================================================
# .gitignore for a project with source files directly in a 'Code' subfolder
# ===================================================================

# -------------------------------------------------------------------
# General C# / .NET / Visual Studio ignores
# These rules are robust and work for most project layouts.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------

# Build output directories inside the 'Code' folder
# This is the most direct way for your specific structure.
Code/[Bb]in/
Code/[Oo]bj/

# User-specific settings and caches
# The '/**/' part makes sure to catch it even if it's nested deeper.
**/.vs/
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

# Rider / ReSharper specific files
**/.idea/
_ReSharper*/
*.[Rr]e[Ss]harper
*.DotSettings.user

# NuGet Packages folder and cache files
# These are restored automatically.
**/[Pp]ackages/
!**/[Pp]ackages/build/ # An exception to the rule above
*.nupkg
project.lock.json
project.assets.json

# Other temporary files
*.log
*.tlog

# -------------------------------------------------------------------
# TestData folder - Nothing to ignore by default
# -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test data files (.in2, .txt, etc.) should be versioned.
# If you generate output files here, add rules below.
# Example: TestData/*.out


# -------------------------------------------------------------------
# A more general (and often better) alternative to the specific rules above.
# The following two lines can replace 'Code/[Bb]in/' and 'Code/[Oo]bj/'.
# They will ignore ANY bin or obj folder, ANYWHERE in the project.
# This is useful if you add more projects in the future.
# Uncomment them if you prefer this more flexible approach.
#
# **/[Bb]in/
# **/[Oo]bj/
#
# -------------------------------------------------------------------